[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114267,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surgical ciliated cyst is a benign cyst caused by the traumatic implantation, usually surgical, of respiratory epithelium in the gnathic bones.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114268,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114269,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DA05.Y Other specified cysts of oral or facial-neck region</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114270,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> surgical ciliated cyst of the maxilla; postoperative maxillary cyst (if maxillary location); (respiratory) implantation cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114271,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114272,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surgical ciliated cysts arise in the gnathic bones, most commonly in the posterior maxilla {6936541; 12524623}. They are very rare in the mandible.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114273,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surgical ciliated cysts may be asymptomatic or present with swelling, pain, or tenderness {3143772; 27478654}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Radiographs show a well-demarcated unilocular radiolucency of the jaws. Approximately 60% of cases are at least partially surrounded by a corticated margin. Occasional large lesions in the maxilla may fill the sinus or be multilocular {3466125; 6936541}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114274,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surgical ciliated cysts are rare {27478654; 31093791}. There is no sex predilection, and the most common age range is the fifth to sixth decades of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114275,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cysts develop from entrapped sinus or nasal mucosa in the jawbones after trauma or surgery. These inciting factors include, but are not limited to, Caldwell&ndash;Luc and Le&nbsp;Fort&nbsp;1 procedures, sinus surgery, maxillary fracture, midface osteotomy, or traumatic tooth extraction {11887151; 15953915; 25109584}. Mandibular cases are generally caused by implantation of sinus epithelium by contaminated instruments, or transfer of epithelium with autologous nasal osteocartilaginous grafts for chin augmentation {11887151; 15953915; 25109584; 33096262}. The cyst usually develops after a long latent period, the reported delay being as long as 20&nbsp;years after the causative surgery {27478654}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114276,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is thought that the implanted epithelium forms a cyst cavity due to persistent mucous secretion. In this respect, some regard the lesion as a type of mucous retention cyst {3466125}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114277,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions are often fragmented but show a cyst wall of variable thickness. The lumen may contain mucinous material.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114278,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cyst is lined by pseudostratified ciliated columnar (respiratory-type) epithelium. Areas of squamous metaplasia or simple cuboidal cells may be seen {3125266}. Mucous (goblet) cells are common. The cyst wall is composed of loose fibrous connective tissue, which may be inflamed. Areas of subepithelial fibrosis or hyalinization are frequent {3143772; 3466125}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114279,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114280,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114281,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a history of previous surgery; a radiolucent, well-demarcated cyst; respiratory epithelial lining.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114282,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114283,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Treatment is simple enucleation and recurrences are rare.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:15:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]